{
  "_about": "The places on the sea chart (Robin, 2026-11-20: 'Big islands with several biomes each, and the chart to sail between them'). Today there is one: Crab Cay, the starter island, with the pirate town on it (Robin, 2026-11-20: 'Make the starter island a pirate town, and the other part of the island beginner friendly with low level mobs'). A new hero starts in `start`, at `wake`, and wakes there after a fall. `home` is the town's outline: no monster comes for him inside it, his health comes back fast, the stall stands there and gets new pieces when he comes in from outside. `biomes` are the grounds of the place, each an outline with a name and its levels, the ones that lie inside another first; the screen says the name when he walks into one. A zone keeps `count` monsters of one kind inside its box; `level` is the Art Director's word for how hard that part is meant to be. Sailing is from a dock (he must stand near `dock`, and steps ashore at the other place's `arrive`); with one place there is nowhere to sail yet. The layout is the Art Director's: tools/place-from-art.mjs writes `land` (where one can stand), `water`, `solids` (circles to walk round), `boxes` (houses, the stall), `dock`, `arrive`, `wake`, `home`, `biomes`, the chest's and the stall's spot and the zones from his place.json; never by hand. Names are Victor, GD's placeholders (docs/names.md).",
